        "math_academy_id": "q-183757",
        "problem": "Describe the set $S={12,9,6,3,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\n15-3n\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n12,\\,9,\\,6,\\,3,\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=-3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =-3 \\\\  & =9-12 \\\\  & =6-9 \\\\  & =\u22ef\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =12+(n-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =12-3n+3 \\\\  & =15-3n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={15-3n\\,:\\,n\\in N}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
